\title{Defining functions in Disco}
\date{2026-03-09T11:52:40Z}
\tag{discrete}
\tag{draft}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{We have [previously seen how to define functions in Disco](http://ozark.hendrix.edu/~yorgey/forest/002K/index.xml). Here are a few more examples.}

\pre\verb<<<|
g : Bool -> N
g(T) = 5
g(F) = 17

h : N -> N
h(n) = 2n

l : N -> Bool
l(3n) = False
l(3n + 1) = True
l(3n + 2) = True

j : N -> N
j(3n) = 2n+5
j(3n+1) = n^2
j(3n+2) = 17
<<<

\p{And we can still use the \code{:table} command to get Disco to show a table of example input-output values for a function.}

